mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&lt;</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></div>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"157\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>144</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"158\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c7D TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo maxsize=\"1.623em\" minsize=\"1.623em\">}</mo></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></div></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Sun, Oct 11th @ 3:31 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:19</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-181976",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14116619/assets/11ec43034f97e66840da012f3beaf2d933fb03cfbe69f510ca5b68f1fd861f83.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.",
      "worked_solution": "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x+1.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x+1\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\ny>-x+1.\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y>-x+1}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
